# CODEOWNERS
#
# One maintainer, so this file is mostly a statement of intent and a template
# for a team repo: it is what makes GitHub require Ahmed's review on anything
# touching delivery-critical paths, and it shows how you'd slice ownership
# by directory on a bigger team (platform folks own gitops/ and charts/,
# app developers own app/, security/platform owns the workflows).

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                           @fakhfakhahmed

# The delivery pipeline itself — changes here can push arbitrary code to
# every environment, so they get the tightest scrutiny.
/.github/workflows/         @fakhfakhahmed
/.github/dependabot.yml     @fakhfakhahmed

# GitOps source of truth — anyone who can merge here can change what's
# running in prod (subject to app-prod's manual-sync gate).
/gitops/                    @fakhfakhahmed

# The Helm chart that every environment deploys.
/charts/                    @fakhfakhahmed

# The application itself.
/app/                       @fakhfakhahmed

# Documentation can be looser in a real team, but is still owned here to
# keep README/LEARN/docs accurate as the pipeline evolves.
/docs/                      @fakhfakhahmed
README.md                   @fakhfakhahmed
LEARN.md                    @fakhfakhahmed
